description.to:
Define the immutable baseline artifact: canonical JSON plus deterministic Markdown, under a series identified by evaluation-contract version.

Fingerprint: scanner commit; corpus/gold digest; contract version; taxonomy and adapter-map digests; dependency-lock digest; all materialized source SHAs; review-state and status counts with provenance; deterministic configuration including AI disabled.

The artifact also embeds:

- baseline-readiness result and invariant versions;
- accepted canonical counts and packet diversity by layer;
- migration-incomplete counts by reason;
- metric computability states and denominators;
- declared capability coverage as diagnostic metadata, never an adjusted recall denominator;
- `predecessor`, with series 1 permitting `none`.

JSON is the source artifact. Markdown is generated deterministically from it and CI verifies no drift. Materialization validation reuses existing manifest-SHA checks and records their results.
